---
title: About DCRP
---
The Digital Civic Resilience Project responds to gaps in the civil society landscape, specifically when civil society organizations (CSOs) face significant threat or closure. This USG funding freeze has had grave implications for CSOs around the world—in particular, the loss of their data and knowledge for future action, as well as the risk posed by unsecured data. DCRP works to preserve this information to avoid the loss of institutional and generational learning, and to provide end of life cycle and resilience support to civil society more broadly. DCRP does not aim to own or host this information, but to act as a convener and create a network of interested partners, among academic institutions and civil society, to safeguard threatened data and knowledge.
